                        <tr>
                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is 46 mL/min/1.73m², which is within the reference range but at the lower end, indicating mildly to moderately reduced kidney function (CKD stage 3a). This is not unexpected in an 87-year-old and should be monitored, especially if there are comorbidities or nephrotoxic medications.</td>
